# registration · TIES

Register once. The holder is the constant: every later entry in your register says who.
Answer in your own words as one combined block; hash the block; the hash goes on line 1 of your
register under this label. The content stays with you. Only the label, the hash and the time are public.

The interview (bin/operator-register): frame, field, question.

physical	government_name	Government name
physical	contact	Contact info
physical	twofa_device	Device like a cell phone, in case of 2FA needed
virtual	device	Computer or device you use (the one you are using at the time is okay)
virtual	username	Username on that system
institution	institution	Institution
institution	institution_purpose	Its operational purpose, mission and what the organization does
role	roles_responsibilities	Your operator roles and responsibilities
role	performance	Your performance: how you are evaluated, what you need to deliver for good performance eval purposes
role	processes	Structured processes that cross your worldline in your operational activity
worldline	worldline_purpose	What your actual worldline is, means to you, its purpose and focus

